# The "styles.content.getContent" override, as an opt-in component of its own.
#
# It is an installation wide rendering change: it redefines a global TypoScript
# object path for every page of the site, not only for the pages of this
# extension. Three academic extensions ship a byte identical copy of it, so a
# site that enables all three used to assign it three times. It is therefore a
# component set of its own - "fgtclb/academic-programs-content-load" - which the
# aggregate set depends on so that a site using the aggregate keeps what it had.
#
# The page template of the page type this extension registers renders this very
# path with "f:cObject", and that ViewHelper throws when the path is undefined.
# A site that takes the content elements without this component therefore has to
# define "styles.content.getContent" itself before it uses the page type.
#
# @todo Recheck this. Is this really safe to be enabled per default ? Or does this eventually need documentation for
# @todo systems not using default fluid-styled-content rendering or bootstrap package or similar ?
# @todo Also duplicated in other academic extensions ?!
styles.content {
  getContent < styles.content.get
  getContent {
    select.where = {#colPos}=0
  }
}
